SUMMARY:Beginning Genealogy Workshop
DTSTART:20260909T090000
DTEND:20260909T110000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:413cf660bb2d1100dd91559b7d5479@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Begin your genealogy research with Lisa Swigert\, a Berkshire 
 OLLI (Osher Lifelong Learning Institute) instructor for four years. Her ov
 er forty years’ experience in genealogical research has proven to be a u
 seful resource for those interested in researching their family history. I
 n a one-day workshop\, Lisa teaches topics ranging from getting started an
 d organizing your research to finding the resources you need to answer you
 r research questions. This course is perfect for the beginning genealogist
  as well as for people getting back into their family history research. We
  will offer an advanced workshop later this year to provide in-depth guide
 lines on researching your Revolutionary War ancestors.\n\nSources: The Ber
 kshires\nEvent page: https://berkshires.org/events-old/beginning-genealogy
 -workshop/
LOCATION:250th Celebration Committee of Adams\, PO Box 251\, Adams\, 01220
URL:https://berkshires.org/events-old/beginning-genealogy-workshop/
END:VEVENT
