DESCRIPTION:💃 SALSA CLASSES ARE BACK THIS SEPTEMBER! Our next 6-week Sa
 lsa series starts September 8 & 10 at the Larcom Theatre. Choose Tuesday o
 r Thursday nights and the class that fits your experience level. BEGINNER 
 1A — FOUNDATIONS Tuesdays at 7:25 PM or Thursdays at 6:20 PM Brand new t
 o Salsa? Start here! Learn On 2 timing\, basic steps\, partner connection
 \, turns\, cross-body leads\, and foundational patterns. No previous exper
 ience necessary. BEGINNER 1B — ESSENTIALS Tuesdays at 6:20 PM or Thursda
 ys at 8:30 PM Ready for the next step? Build on the foundations from 1A wh
 ile improving timing\, connection\, leading and following technique\, tran
 sitions\, musicality\, and beginner patterns. Completion of Beginner 1A or
  equivalent experience is required. COUPLES BEGINNER 1B Tuesdays at 8:30 P
 M Want to learn together without rotating partners? This class is designed
  specifically for couples. Stay with the partner you came with while build
 ing connection\, technique\, smoother transitions\, and expanded Beginner 
 1B patterns. Beginner 1A or equivalent experience required. 6 weeks. One n
 ight a week. Lots of Salsa. We extend a special invitation for ‘leads’
  to join\, as their participation will help ensure a robust presence of po
 tential partner leads. ​ Grab your spot and join us on the dance floor t
 his September! Thelarcom.org/learnsalsa For questions about the class\, em
 ail: donnie@thelarcom.org LARCOM THEATRE\, 13 Wallis St\, Beverly MA\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/latin-
 night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/2026-09-24/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/latin-night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/
 2026-09-24/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20260924T110000
DTEND:20260924T170000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:7cf6abe8f4a7a0a50df2d755fa42bd@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-09-24/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-09-24/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Open Studios: Fiona Sinéad Brehony\, GAR Environmental / Installa
 tion Artist
DTSTART:20260924T140000
DTEND:20260924T160000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:e3b3ded10154f68e7ad1fafe094add@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join Fiona Sinéad Brehony\, the 2026 GAR Environmental / Inst
 allation Artist\, to see her work in progress at Ocean Alliance on Thursda
 y\, September 17 or Thursday\, September 24 from 2-4 pm. This residency of
 fers Brehony an opportunity to explore Gloucester Harbor through Richard W
 hite’s concept of the organic machine\, simultaneously a natural system 
 and human infrastructure\, yet also something so vast and distributed it e
 xceeds our ability to fully grasp it. She will engage in acts of listening
 \, watching and writing to see what emerges\, inviting participants in for
  gatherings where ideas can transform collectively. Working with Ocean All
 iance’s whale song archives\, she hopes to develop poetic work that expl
 ores ocean presence\, waters shared with whales\, where freshwater meets s
 alt and interaction shifts from intimate to incomprehensible.\n\nSources: 
 North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/open-studios-
 fiona-sinead-brehony-gar-environmental-installation-artist/2026-09-24/
LOCATION:Ocean Alliance\, 32 Horton Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930-1836
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/open-studios-fiona-sinead-brehony-gar-
 environmental-installation-artist/2026-09-24/
END:VEVENT
