BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Latin Night! Learn Salsa – Dance Lessons
DTSTART:20261006T182000
DTEND:20261006T213000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:2852e9cf3453ca3dbbcbc0aa035651@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:💃 SALSA CLASSES ARE BACK THIS SEPTEMBER! Our next 6-week Sa
 lsa series starts September 8 & 10 at the Larcom Theatre. Choose Tuesday o
 r Thursday nights and the class that fits your experience level. BEGINNER 
 1A — FOUNDATIONS Tuesdays at 7:25 PM or Thursdays at 6:20 PM Brand new t
 o Salsa? Start here! Learn On 2 timing\, basic steps\, partner connection
 \, turns\, cross-body leads\, and foundational patterns. No previous exper
 ience necessary. BEGINNER 1B — ESSENTIALS Tuesdays at 6:20 PM or Thursda
 ys at 8:30 PM Ready for the next step? Build on the foundations from 1A wh
 ile improving timing\, connection\, leading and following technique\, tran
 sitions\, musicality\, and beginner patterns. Completion of Beginner 1A or
  equivalent experience is required. COUPLES BEGINNER 1B Tuesdays at 8:30 P
 M Want to learn together without rotating partners? This class is designed
  specifically for couples. Stay with the partner you came with while build
 ing connection\, technique\, smoother transitions\, and expanded Beginner 
 1B patterns. Beginner 1A or equivalent experience required. 6 weeks. One n
 ight a week. Lots of Salsa. We extend a special invitation for ‘leads’
  to join\, as their participation will help ensure a robust presence of po
 tential partner leads. ​ Grab your spot and join us on the dance floor t
 his September! Thelarcom.org/learnsalsa For questions about the class\, em
 ail: donnie@thelarcom.org LARCOM THEATRE\, 13 Wallis St\, Beverly MA\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/latin-
 night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/2026-10-06/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/latin-night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/
 2026-10-06/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:CAM Studio Art: Design and Print the Folly Cove Way
DTSTART:20261007T130000
DTEND:20261007T160000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:31fbf285ef16e8a04a9cfb2bf04cca@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into the spirit of the legendary Folly Cove Designers and
  learn the art of block printing with artist Mary Rhinelander in this four
 -week course. This class blends design fundamentals\, creative play\, and 
 the rich history of Cape Ann’s iconic design collective. Referencing her
  unpublished book\, Design and How\, you’ll explore the principles of de
 sign that Virginia Lee Demetrios taught her students—selecting a theme a
 nd exploring it deeply through clarity of line\, rhythm\, repetition\, and
  pattern—and you will discover how her timeless ideas can elevate your o
 wn artistic voice. Each week builds your confidence as you sketch\, carve
 \, and print your way towards an original finished artwork. Please note: T
 his class has four sessions. Mary Rhinelander is a professional artist wit
 h an MFA in printmaking. Gloucester is in her DNA\, starting with great-gr
 andparents who spent summers on Eastern Point. She lives in East Glouceste
 r\, in a yellow clapboard house once known as “The Summer Art House” w
 here painter Theresa Bernstein and her painter/printmaker husband\, Willia
 m Meyerowitz\, spent many decades (starting in 1924). Having purchased her
  home directly from their estate\, William’s etching press is still happ
 ily living in the sun-filled basement studio. Mary has had many solo and g
 roup shows and her work is in both public and private collections. She has
  painted murals\, designed logos and book covers\, illustrated for a varie
 ty of publications\, and taught students of all ages. In 2004 she founded 
 Mermade Press\, a fine art card business. With a deep affinity for the Fol
 ly Cove Designers and Virginia Lee Demetrios in particular\, it has been M
 ary’s great pleasure to bring block printing workshops into Cape Ann’s
  public schools with the support of CAM and the Gloucester Education Found
 ation.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/
 event/cam-studio-art-design-and-print-the-folly-cove-way/2026-10-07/
LOCATION:Cape Ann Museum\, 27 Pleasant Street\, Gloucester\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/cam-studio-art-design-and-print-the-fo
 lly-cove-way/2026-10-07/
END:VEVENT
