BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:En Plein Air Sketch Classes with Sue Wheeler
DTSTART:20261008T080000
DTEND:20261008T170000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:cba67c92fb5801fac85999baae3fa1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:From stick figure doodlers to first-rate talents\, join us for
  a seaside\, En Plein Air sketch class with Sue Wheeler of Arts Abound in 
 Magnolia. All skill levels are welcome! This two-hour session includes a 3
 0-minute beginner sketch lesson. All you need to bring is a sketchbook\, p
 encils\, a ruler\, and an eraser. Please note: watercolors\, pastels\, oil
 s\, or acrylics are not permitted on the Museum grounds. Attendees who wis
 h to tour the Hammond Castle Museum after this class are entitled to a 20%
  discount on a self-guided tour. Tour tickets may be purchased in the Muse
 um Shop before 2:30 pm on the day of this class. Class Schedule: Thursday 
 Plein Air Sketch classes: 1:00 pm – 3:00 pm. May:14 June: 11 July 23: (6
  – 8 pm) August: 6 September: 10 October: 8 Saturday En Plein Air Sketch
  classes: 9:30 am- 11:30 am. May: 9 June: 20 July:18 August: 1 September: 
 5 October: 3 All classes are $25 each. Museum Member savings apply. Weathe
 r-dependent\; classes may be canceled\, and reservations will be refunded 
 if necessary. About Sue Wheeler: Sue has a lifetime of making art through 
 various mediums from delectable pastries to abstracts in pastels\, waterco
 lor\, and acrylics. She enjoys using her creative flair in quilting and in
 terior design as well. Sue graduated from the University of Denver with a 
 Bachelor’s in business with a focus on hospitality management and earned
  an associate’s degree from the Culinary Institute of America. Following
  her tenure as a pastry chef in New Hampshire\, Sue returned to school for
  a certificate in graphic design and put her talents to use as a designer 
 in the book publishing and art publishing industries in Vermont. In early 
 2019\, Sue opened her own gallery and studio\, Arts Abound in Magnolia Vil
 lage\, MA\, as an artistic haven for local artists. Through the gallery\, 
 over 30 artists featured their creative works\, ranging from paintings\, h
 and-painted silk scarves\, silver jewelry\, and more. Sue also ran many wo
 rkshops and classes featuring many of the artists. Often\, Sue would work 
 late into the night\, painting in her Arts Abound studio. After closing th
 e gallery in 2022\, Sue continued to offer the often sold-out painting cla
 sses\, taught by some of the Arts Abound artists. Sue has studied under nu
 merous artists to learn watercolor\, acrylic painting\, cold wax & oil\, a
 nd collage. Her goals for the Hammond Castle Museum sketch classes are to 
 engage those who are new to the world of art and reinvigorate those who ha
 ven’t picked up a blank canvas or sketch pad in a long time. Sue’s phi
 losophy on the creative process encourages you to be less concerned about 
 the final product and instead to enjoy the journey of creativity and get l
 ost in the moment. Once you find yourself in your work\, you may just be s
 urprised!\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.o
 rg/event/en-plein-air-sketch-classes-with-sue-wheeler-10/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/en-plein-air-sketch-classes-with-sue-w
 heeler-10/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fiona Brehony Explores Gloucester Harbor\, Whale Song\, and the Li
 ving Memory of Water
DTSTART:20261008T170000
DTEND:20261008T180000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:fb0b83389776cf2c7bb91da6624bec@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:GOETEMANN ARTIST RESIDENCY BRINGS MANCHESTER-BASED ARTIST AND 
 WRITER TO GLOUCESTER OPENING TALK: THURSDAY SEPTEMBER 10 / (RNAC 5-6 PM) O
 PEN STUDIO: THURSDAY 2-4 PM 9/17 (OCEAN ALLIANCE) WALK/LISTEN: THURSDAY 9/
 24 2-4 PM (OCEAN ALLIANCE) CLOSING TALK: THURSDAY 10/1 4-5 PM (OCEAN ALLIA
 NCE) Gloucester\, MA – What can water remember? What stories are held wi
 thin a harbor\, a river\, or an ocean and whose stories are we able to hea
 r? These questions are at the heart of the work of artist and writer Fiona
  Brehony\, the current Goetemann Artist-in-Residence at Rocky Neck Art Col
 ony. Based in Manchester\, Britain\, Brehony works across moving image\, s
 ound\, and performance\, collaborating with scientists\, composers\, histo
 rians\, and communities to create poetic and inquisitive works that explor
 e the relationships between people\, places\, and waterways. During her re
 sidency in Gloucester\, Brehony is turning her attention to Gloucester Har
 bor\, exploring the harbor as both a natural ecosystem and a human-made in
 frastructure. Her work is informed by historian Richard White’s concept 
 of the “organic machine” – a landscape that is simultaneously natura
 l and shaped by human activity. This idea offers a way of approaching the 
 harbor not as a backdrop\, but as a complex living system in which water\,
  industry\, infrastructure\, human communities\, and other species are con
 tinually shaping one another. Brehony’s approach of thinking with water 
 considers water not simply as a subject or environment\, but as a material
  that connects bodies\, places\, histories\, and species. Drawing on Astri
 da Neimanis’s concept of Bodies of Water\, she is interested in the ways
  human bodies are already materially entangled with the waters around them
 . In Gloucester\, this raises questions about how we might listen to a har
 bor as bodies already implicated in its waters – and how whale song\, hu
 man voices\, harbor infrastructure\, and the movement of water might becom
 e part of a shared\, though uneven\, ecological and acoustic body. Her res
 idency includes a collaboration with Ocean Alliance\, engaging with the or
 ganization’s extensive archives of whale song to develop poetic work on 
 the ocean’s presence and the waters shared with whales. Brehony is explo
 ring the ocean as a living archive – one that carries ecological history
 \, community memory\, and evidence of the ways human and non-human lives i
 ntersect. “Water can hold histories that we don’t know how to access\,
 ” Brehony says. “I’m interested in what happens when we listen close
 ly to a place\, and in what might emerge when those acts of listening beco
 me collective.” The residency extends ideas developed through Brehony’
 s ongoing Liquid History project\, workshops and soundwalks approaching ri
 vers as living archives of social and ecological memory\, previously focus
 ed on the River Irk in North Manchester. In Gloucester\, that inquiry expa
 nds from river to harbor and ocean\, where the scale of water – and the 
 number of lives entangled within it – becomes harder to grasp. The publi
 c is invited to a series of gatherings and events during her time in Glouc
 ester. Brehony is an AHRC-funded doctoral candidate researching the River 
 Irk in North Manchester as a living site of cultural heritage and has spen
 t this summer as artist in residence with the Norwegian Institute for Natu
 re Research in Oslo\, developing Water Symphony\, following the city’s f
 jord\, rivers\, and waterways as a medium for exploring urban justice. Her
  work has been commissioned by the Whitworth Art Gallery\, the University 
 of Oxford\, PRiSM at the Royal Northern College of Music\, and Creswell Cr
 ags Museum\, and supported by Arts Council England and the AHRC. The Goete
 mann Artist Residency Program is a program of Rocky Neck Art Colony\, brin
 ging contemporary artists to Gloucester to engage with the community\, exp
 lore the region’s rich cultural and environmental landscape\, and develo
 p new work in response to place. For more information about Fiona Brehony
 ’s residency\, upcoming public programs\, and the Goetemann Artist Resid
 ency Program\, visit Rocky Neck Art Colony at rockyneckartcolony.org.\n\nS
 ources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/fiona
 -brehony-explores-gloucester-harbor-whale-song-and-the-living-memory-of-wa
 ter/2026-10-08/
LOCATION:Rocky Neck
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/fiona-brehony-explores-gloucester-harb
 or-whale-song-and-the-living-memory-of-water/2026-10-08/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Latin Night! Learn Salsa – Dance Lessons
DTSTART:20261008T182000
DTEND:20261008T213000
DTSTAMP:20260830T154120Z
UID:9000398779a5a22256825e7e19dbdc@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:💃 SALSA CLASSES ARE BACK THIS SEPTEMBER! Our next 6-week Sa
 lsa series starts September 8 & 10 at the Larcom Theatre. Choose Tuesday o
 r Thursday nights and the class that fits your experience level. BEGINNER 
 1A — FOUNDATIONS Tuesdays at 7:25 PM or Thursdays at 6:20 PM Brand new t
 o Salsa? Start here! Learn On 2 timing\, basic steps\, partner connection
 \, turns\, cross-body leads\, and foundational patterns. No previous exper
 ience necessary. BEGINNER 1B — ESSENTIALS Tuesdays at 6:20 PM or Thursda
 ys at 8:30 PM Ready for the next step? Build on the foundations from 1A wh
 ile improving timing\, connection\, leading and following technique\, tran
 sitions\, musicality\, and beginner patterns. Completion of Beginner 1A or
  equivalent experience is required. COUPLES BEGINNER 1B Tuesdays at 8:30 P
 M Want to learn together without rotating partners? This class is designed
  specifically for couples. Stay with the partner you came with while build
 ing connection\, technique\, smoother transitions\, and expanded Beginner 
 1B patterns. Beginner 1A or equivalent experience required. 6 weeks. One n
 ight a week. Lots of Salsa. We extend a special invitation for ‘leads’
  to join\, as their participation will help ensure a robust presence of po
 tential partner leads. ​ Grab your spot and join us on the dance floor t
 his September! Thelarcom.org/learnsalsa For questions about the class\, em
 ail: donnie@thelarcom.org LARCOM THEATRE\, 13 Wallis St\, Beverly MA\n\nSo
 urces: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/latin-
 night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/2026-10-08/
LOCATION:Larcom Theatre\, 13 Wallis Street\, Beverly\, MA\, 01915
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/latin-night-learn-salsa-dance-lessons/
 2026-10-08/
END:VEVENT
